<SiteLayout title="About">
  <header class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Quantum Flytrap, 2019–2022. Virtual Lab, ongoing.</h1>
  </header>
  <section class="prose">
    <h2>Current stewardship</h2>
    <p>Virtual Lab is owned and supported by Piotr Migdał and Klem Jankiewicz. It remains free to use and will stay online indefinitely.</p>

    <h2>The startup</h2>
    <p>Quantum Flytrap was founded by quantum physicist Piotr Migdał and designer Klem Jankiewicz to build accessible interfaces for quantum technologies. The startup closed in October 2022.</p>
    <p>Its work included Virtual Lab, Quantum Game, browser-based quantum numerics, and Pulser Studio for Pasqal.</p>

    <h2>People</h2>
    <p>The core team included Piotr Migdał, Klem Jankiewicz, and lead software engineer Paweł Grabarz, with contributions from Agata Rakowiecka, Bijaya Dangol, Chiara Decaroli, Kamila Stępniowska, Alicja Głuszek, Philippe Cochin, and others. Artur Ekert served as an advisor.</p>

    <p><a class="text-link" href="/blog/closing-quantum-flytrap/">Read the 2022 closing note →</a></p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
